# Never commit credentials
.env
*.env
env
secrets/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/

# Per-node context (gitignored)
CLAUDE.local.md
nodes.local
__pycache__/
.mesh/

# knowledge/ = node-local research + gossiped-tier perception (surveys, findings). NOT the genome.
# Operator decision 2026-06-13: research docs carry too much node-specifics (real IPs, server configs)
# to belong in a PUBLIC genome — the prior "durable docs stay tracked" policy is exactly how a phaedra
# WireGuard-server doc leaked (7ba754f). The whole dir is node-local now: it propagates node-to-node
# (gossip/trace/scp), never via git. Genome = generic skeleton (scripts/ + docs/ + CLAUDE.md). To share
# a genuinely-generic lesson, promote it to docs/ DELIBERATELY — never auto-commit from knowledge/.
# The tier itself lives at ~/.mesh/knowledge (a git repo, its own private remote); this rule
# only keeps it from re-appearing INSIDE the genome. A clone did exactly that until
# 2026-08-21 — wedged at the founding commit, all 130 tracked files deleted, 2 stale
# untracked drafts, never pushed, and gitignored so no genome-side check could see it.
# `mesh-knowledge-publish` drives the durability lane and reports a second clone at this path.
knowledge/

# Ephemeral verify/check artifacts a mind drops in the repo root for a single verification pass.
# They carry node-specifics and go stale fast (the genome moves past them — e.g. .verify-notify-actuator
# described a probe line that's since been refactored to `mesh-notify --check`). NOT the genome. Without
# this, a `git add -A` during a push-prep thread sweeps them into the PUBLIC genome.
.verify-*
doc-drift-*
verify-rotation-*

# opencode node-local plugin/state dir — never the genome (would leak local config + break plant)
.opencode/

# antigravitycli node-local state dir — never the genome
.antigravitycli/

# Scratch dev artifacts a mind drops in the repo ROOT while iterating (camera frames from cam/PIL
# motion-gate dev, throwaway test scripts). Node-specific + stale-fast, never the genome. Without
# this they show as untracked → sync-tools [genome-strand] flags them as blocking the next pull, and
# a `git add -A` during push-prep would sweep binary cruft into the PUBLIC genome. Anchored to root
# (`/…`) so a legit image/script in a subdir is never hidden. (tuner-eye PIL work 721d262 left these.)
/scratch_*
/img*.jpg
/frame*.jpg
/photo*.jpg
# root-level bash xtrace/debug logs (`set -x` output a mind pipes to `_tr.log` while
# iterating). Untracked, they keep the tree DIRTY, which DISABLES fitness auto-revert
# ("alarmed, not reverted") — a stray trace silently defeats the safety net. (2026-07-16)
/_*.log

# job lane: the funnel is the operator's live job-hunt statistics and this repo is PUBLIC
# (github.com/genaforvena/lte-workstation, CC0 by intent). The lane CODE is public; his
# application/rejection/interview counts are not. Operator decision 2026-08-29.
job/FUNNEL.md
